{{!--
  One item icon, ringed in its rarity's colour (D-676).

  **A ring is a SECOND carrier, not the only one** - the name beside it
  already takes the rarity's colour on every surface that uses this partial
  (D-634), and the item sheet says the rarity in words. That is what makes a
  colour-only ring legitimate here (D5, CLAUDE.md SS22).

  The ring is an OUTLINE rather than a border: the row icons are `flex: none`
  at exactly 20px with no space budgeted for a frame, and the spell row's grid
  track is a hard 20px, so a border would shrink the art or reflow the row.
  Common takes no rarity class and falls back to a neutral iron ring, so every
  icon is framed the same way and only the colour changes.
--}}
{{#if img}}
<span class="azeroth-icon {{#if rarityClass}}{{rarityClass}}{{else}}azeroth-rarity-common{{/if}}">
  <img src="{{img}}" alt="">
</span>
{{else}}
<span class="azeroth-icon azeroth-icon--empty"></span>
{{/if}}
